{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowCorners","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungLatticeUpOperator","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BallotNumbers","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableauBot"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_eq_ballot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_eq_ballot","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L178-L208","doc":"**The two-row standard-tableau count IS the ballot number**, for every `k ≤ m`.\n\n    #SYT (m, k) = ballot (m + k) k\n\nOuter induction on `k`, inner induction on `m` from `k` upward (`Nat.le_induction`): the `k < m`\nstep needs the result at the *same* `k` with a smaller `m`, which an induction on `k` alone\ncannot supply.\n\nThe two `ballot` facts consumed are exactly the two the corpus already had: `ballot_succ_succ`\nfor the generic step, and `ballot_boundary_zero` for the `k = m` boundary, where the term that\nmust vanish is `ballot (2j+1) (j+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_rec_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_rec_eq","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L166-L174","doc":"**`k = m > 0`: only the row-1 corner.**  `(0, m-1)` is *not* removable here — the cell below\nit is present — which is exactly what makes the boundary case work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_rec_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_rec_lt","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L154-L164","doc":"**`0 < k < m`: two corners.**  Successor form: `k = j + 1`, `m = M + 1`, `j + 1 ≤ M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_zero","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L141-L152","doc":"**One row, one tableau.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.twoRow_zero_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.twoRow_zero_zero","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L133-L139","doc":"`twoRow 0 0` is the empty diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row1_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row1_succ","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L124-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row0_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row0_succ","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L120-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row1","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L96-L111","doc":"Erasing the end of row 1 shortens row 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row0","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L79-L94","doc":"Erasing the end of row 0 shortens row 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.sum_cornerTwoRow_expand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.sum_cornerTwoRow_expand","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L70-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.cornerCells_twoRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.cornerCells_twoRow","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L65-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.mem_cornerTwoRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.mem_cornerTwoRow","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L60-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.cornerTwoRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.cornerTwoRow","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L56-L58","doc":"The removable corners of `twoRow m k`.  Mirrors `addableTwoRow`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}